Hi Chaoyi,

The fix is right. The Fixes: tag names the wrong commit.

658ebeac3351 ("accel/rocket: Add IOCTL for BO creation") touches six
files: drivers/accel/rocket/Makefile, rocket_drv.c, rocket_drv.h,
rocket_gem.c, rocket_gem.h and include/uapi/drm/rocket_accel.h. It does
not touch rocket_job.c at all.

rocket_job.c is added by its immediate child, 0810d5ad88a1
("accel/rocket: Add job submission IOCTL"), and that commit adds
rocket_job_handle_irq(), the line you are changing, and the
rocket_reset() detach that already passes core->iommu_group. So:

  Fixes: 0810d5ad88a1 ("accel/rocket: Add job submission IOCTL")

which is also the tag on ZhaoJinming's copy of the same one line
change [1], posted in June bundled with runtime PM guards for the IRQ
handler. The leak is still there in mainline and in linux-next today.

I have the same one line change on a branch here and am not posting
it. Yours came first as a standalone patch, and a third copy of a one
liner would be noise.

No Tested-by from me yet, because it would not be true. The patch is
carried here on next-20260911 and builds clean, but I have not booted
a kernel with it. Respin with the corrected tag and I will run it on
RK3576 (ROCK 4D) and reply with one.

One conflict worth naming, because it has to be resolved either way.
Our RK3576 series has a patch that moves this exact line, unchanged,
into a new helper: "accel/rocket: factor the completion tail out of
the IRQ handler", v12 05/14 [2]. Whichever of the two lands first, the
other needs a rebase. The v12 cover asks Tomeu which he would rather
take, but it names Zhao's copy only. It should have named yours.

Igor Paunovic offered on 2026-07-29, and again on 2026-09-09 [3], to
test a standalone respin of Zhao's patch or to post it himself. No
answer to either so far. Yours is already standalone, so a v2 of it
with the corrected tag is the shortest way out for all three copies.

